WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.106
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.406 --> 00:00:08.920
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:15.042
Unit eleven: Climate & Environment. Today you will make suggestions with should and could.

4
00:00:15.342 --> 00:00:17.960
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.458
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:24.515
Ecosystem.

7
00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:29.652
Ecosystem means all the plants and animals living together in one area.

8
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.842
The Tonle Sap is an important ecosystem.

9
00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.195
Your turn. Say: Ecosystem.

10
00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:40.116
Ecosystem.

11
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:41.956
Carbon emission.

12
00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:46.888
Carbon emission means gas from cars and factories that warms the Earth.

13
00:00:47.483 --> 00:00:49.808
Cycling reduces carbon emissions.

14
00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:53.591
Your turn. Say: Carbon emission.

15
00:00:56.433 --> 00:00:57.551
Carbon emission.

16
00:00:58.317 --> 00:00:59.457
Recyclable.

17
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:03.727
Recyclable means able to be used again after processing.

18
00:01:04.317 --> 00:01:06.316
Cans and bottles are recyclable.

19
00:01:06.917 --> 00:01:09.929
Your turn. Say: Recyclable.

20
00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:14.116
Recyclable.

21
00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:15.886
Sustainable.

22
00:01:16.883 --> 00:01:20.357
Sustainable means able to continue without harming the planet.

23
00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:22.775
We need sustainable farming.

24
00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:25.722
Your turn. Say: Sustainable.

25
00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:29.707
Sustainable.

26
00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:31.672
Conservation.

27
00:01:32.683 --> 00:01:35.693
Conservation means protecting nature and animals.

28
00:01:36.283 --> 00:01:38.480
Conservation saves forests.

29
00:01:39.083 --> 00:01:41.689
Your turn. Say: Conservation.

30
00:01:44.533 --> 00:01:45.662
Conservation.

31
00:01:46.417 --> 00:01:47.360
Pollution.

32
00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:51.035
Pollution means dirty air, water or land.

33
00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:53.917
Plastic pollution hurts fish.

34
00:01:54.517 --> 00:01:56.983
Your turn. Say: Pollution.

35
00:01:59.833 --> 00:02:00.765
Pollution.

36
00:02:01.517 --> 00:02:03.005
Renewable energy.

37
00:02:04.017 --> 00:02:07.224
Renewable energy means power from sun, wind or water.

38
00:02:07.817 --> 00:02:10.397
Solar panels use renewable energy.

39
00:02:10.983 --> 00:02:14.576
Your turn. Say: Renewable energy.

40
00:02:17.433 --> 00:02:19.386
Renewable energy.

41
00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:21.859
Biodiversity.

42
00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:26.881
Biodiversity means the variety of living things in a place.

43
00:02:27.483 --> 00:02:29.924
Rainforests have great biodiversity.

44
00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:33.552
Your turn. Say: Biodiversity.

45
00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.365
Biodiversity.

46
00:02:39.117 --> 00:02:40.396
Deforestation.

47
00:02:41.383 --> 00:02:44.718
Deforestation means cutting down large areas of forest.

48
00:02:45.317 --> 00:02:47.920
Deforestation destroys animal homes.

49
00:02:48.517 --> 00:02:51.471
Your turn. Say: Deforestation.

50
00:02:54.333 --> 00:02:55.706
Deforestation.

51
00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:57.695
Eco-friendly.

52
00:02:58.683 --> 00:03:01.588
Eco-friendly means not harmful to the environment.

53
00:03:02.183 --> 00:03:04.369
Bamboo straws are eco-friendly.

54
00:03:04.983 --> 00:03:07.775
Your turn. Say: Eco-friendly.

55
00:03:10.633 --> 00:03:11.843
Eco-friendly.

56
00:03:12.583 --> 00:03:13.492
Impact.

57
00:03:14.483 --> 00:03:16.587
Impact means a strong effect.

58
00:03:17.183 --> 00:03:19.287
Plastic has a big impact on the sea.

59
00:03:19.883 --> 00:03:22.303
Your turn. Say: Impact.

60
00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:26.075
Impact.

61
00:03:26.817 --> 00:03:27.667
Preserve.

62
00:03:28.683 --> 00:03:31.403
Preserve means to keep something safe from harm.

63
00:03:32.017 --> 00:03:34.051
We must preserve our forests.

64
00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.488
Your turn. Say: Preserve.

65
00:03:40.333 --> 00:03:41.102
Preserve.

66
00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:45.922
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:46.783 --> 00:03:49.479
Visal, what can teenagers do for the environment?

68
00:03:50.583 --> 00:03:53.535
We should recycle more and use less plastic.

69
00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:57.059
Good. What about energy?

70
00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:02.634
Our school could use renewable energy, like solar panels.

71
00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:04.983
And transport?

72
00:04:06.083 --> 00:04:10.942
We could cycle to school. It cuts carbon emissions and it's eco-friendly.

73
00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.531
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:14.383 --> 00:04:17.881
Grammar focus: should and could for suggestions.

75
00:04:18.181 --> 00:04:19.391
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:20.083 --> 00:04:21.549
We should recycle more.

77
00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:24.473
We could use renewable energy.

78
00:04:25.383 --> 00:04:27.441
Schools should plant more trees.

79
00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:33.154
Use 'should' when you think it is the right thing to do. Use 'could' to give a possible idea.

80
00:04:33.917 --> 00:04:37.742
Be careful! Don't say: We should recycling more.

81
00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:42.350
Say: We should recycle more.

82
00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:45.067
After should or could, use the base verb.

83
00:04:45.867 --> 00:04:48.937
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:49.733 --> 00:04:51.187
Our Planet Needs Us.

85
00:04:51.487 --> 00:04:55.542
Deforestation harms biodiversity and the whole ecosystem.

86
00:04:56.533 --> 00:04:59.903
Pollution from factories and cars also has a big impact.

87
00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:04.037
Choosing renewable energy helps reduce carbon emissions.

88
00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:08.159
We should buy recyclable and eco-friendly products.

89
00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:12.165
Together, we could preserve the environment for the future.

90
00:05:13.267 --> 00:05:17.733
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:18.583 --> 00:05:22.048
We blank use solar energy. It's one idea.

92
00:05:22.348 --> 00:05:25.468
A, could. B, can't. C, mustn't.

93
00:05:29.033 --> 00:05:30.418
The answer is A: could.

94
00:05:31.583 --> 00:05:34.338
Cutting down large areas of forest is blank.

95
00:05:34.638 --> 00:05:39.696
A, deforestation. B, conservation. C, biodiversity.

96
00:05:43.233 --> 00:05:45.895
The answer is A: deforestation.

97
00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:49.746
Power from sun, wind or water is blank.

98
00:05:50.046 --> 00:05:55.476
A, renewable energy. B, pollution. C, carbon emission.

99
00:05:59.033 --> 00:06:02.020
The answer is A: renewable energy.

100
00:06:03.233 --> 00:06:06.199
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:09.607
What can teenagers do to help the environment?

102
00:06:18.417 --> 00:06:19.940
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:27.699
Teenagers should reduce plastic and recycle. We could also plant trees at school and cycle instead of using motorbikes.

104
00:06:27.999 --> 00:06:29.790
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:30.683 --> 00:06:35.692
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and should and could for suggestions.

106
00:06:35.992 --> 00:06:40.386
Today's value is protecting nature. Keep the sea, rivers and forests clean.

107
00:06:40.686 --> 00:06:42.956
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

108
00:06:43.256 --> 00:06:46.152
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

